{
  "id": "1846651706696737",
  "title": "Shh... This Won't Hurt a Bit.",
  "published_at": "2026-10-20T20:59:53Z",
  "url": "https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706696737",
  "content": "It's hard to know if that chill in the air is from the approaching fall breeze, or from the withering glare of Nurse Harrow, who now joins us on the streets of Manhattan. To some, her practices may seem unorthodox, her patients at the Marble Hill Possession Ward cannot say that the results aren't effective. With Leech Therapy, she throws a jar full of leeches that attach to oncoming enemies, draining their health and energy, before crawling back to deliver their haul. Cracking open one of her vials, she releases her Wretched Vapors, possessing her allies with a powerful boost of effectiveness - though subjects should be warned of the side effects when the vapors wear off. To efficiently keep her teammates fighting their best, she loads her syringe full of Healing Needles to inject medicine directly into their veins. And when her patience runs out, she opens her bag to release all the Lurking Terrors captured inside, making her adversaries run for cover. - \"Trust me, I know best.\"\nWith Nurse Harrow joining us today, that marks the end of our City Never Sleeps releases. We want to thank everyone for participating in voting once again, and hope you've been enjoying all the new delights that NYC has to offer.\nCity Never Sleeps Voting Stats:\n- Big Turnout: Over 110 Million votes were cast over the course of the event.\n- Narrow Victory: The closest contest was Baba vs Solomon, decided by a nearly 0.5% difference in votes.\n- Oracle: Only 847 players voted in every round, and only voted for that round's eventual winner.\n- Unlucky: 36,236 players voted in every round, and never once picked that round's winner.\n- Dedication: 22,194 players exclusively voted for Nurse Harrow. One player cast exactly 1000 votes for her.\n- Highly Effective: Nurse Harrow voters consistently proved to have a higher win rate over all other hero voters.",
